    "campaign": "WAGYU FESTIVAL",
    "caption": "Feeling a fancy breakfast?\n\nWhip up this One Skillet Breakfast Steak & Eggs using Margaret River Wagyu Breakfast Steak. Wake up like a champion and tuck into this glorious feast of a first meal. Pair with your choice of orange juice, tea, or coffee, or flutes of mimosas if you’re feeling some bubbly. Grab all the ingredients that you need for this recipe only at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 1 hour\nYield: 2 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFOR THE STEAK MARINADE\n\n2 tbsps. olive oil \n1 tbsp. soy sauce \n1 tbsp. worcestershire sauce \n1 tbsp. dijon mustard \n1 tbsp. thyme \n3 cloves garlic, grated \n1 slab Margaret River Wagyu Breakfast Steak, pat dried\n\nFOR THE OTHER COMPONENTS\n\n1/4 cup olive oil \n2 tbsps. butter\n2 white onions, sliced \n2 red onions, sliced \n2 cups shiitake mushrooms, sliced \n1 cup shimeji mushrooms, trimmed \n2 tbsps. thyme \n2 eggs\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Combine all steak marinade ingredients. Coat Margaret River Wagyu Breakfast Steak with the mixture, and marinate for at least 15 minutes.\n2. Heat up 3 tbsps. olive oil over medium-high heat. Once it's smoking, sear steak until nicely browned on 1 side, about 2 minutes. Flip, then lower heat, and add 2 tbsp. butter. Baste for 3-5 minutes, or until desired doneness. Remove steak from the pan, and cover in foil while cooking the other components.\n3. In the same pan, sauté onions until tender and translucent. When almost there, add remaining butter, and mix in mushrooms. Continue to cook until tender. Season with salt and pepper, and mix in thyme.\n4. Lower the heat, and make 2 wells in the middle for the eggs. Add remaining olive oil, then crack eggs into the wells. Season with salt and pepper. Turn off heat.\n5. Slice the steak against the grain, then place on top of the sauteéd vegetables.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
